  "_skill_md": "---\nname: canva\ndescription: Internal API for canva\nmetadata:\n  author: unbrowse\n  version: \"1.0\"\n  baseUrl: \"https://www.canva.com\"\n  authMethod: \"Session Token (x-csrf-token)\"\n  endpointCount: 6\n  apiType: \"internal\"\n  category: \"web-app\"\n---\n\n# Canva API\n\n> Reverse-engineered internal API. Unofficial — may change without notice.\n\n## Documentation Index\n- `SKILL.md` (this file)\n- `references/REFERENCE.md` (detailed endpoint docs)\n- `references/ENDPOINTS.json` (machine-readable endpoint catalog)\n- `scripts/api.ts` (typed client interface)\n\n## Authentication\nSession Token (x-csrf-token) — Authentication method detected from captured traffic.\n\n### Providing credentials\n- Prefer passing auth as request headers or cookies at call time (do not hardcode secrets into the skill).\n- If executing via an external proxy/executor, pass per-call credentials (cookies and/or headers) so they are not persisted.\n\n## Dependencies\n- Runtime capable of HTTPS requests.\n- If using `scripts/api.ts`: TypeScript toolchain (or transpile to JS).\n\n## Endpoints\n\n### Auth Flow (2)\n- `GET /_ajax/csrf3/ae` — Obtain a CSRF token for Canva API requests.\n- `POST /_ajax/authnflow/auth-dialog-content` — Initiate or continue the Canva authentication flow.\n\n### Data Read (2)\n- `GET /{id}` — Retrieve a specific Canva object by its ID.\n- `GET /{id}/{id}` — Retrieve a nested Canva object using two IDs.\n\n### Data Write (1)\n- `POST /v1/traces` — Send tracing data to Canva for monitoring.\n\n### Core API (1)\n- `POST /_ajax/ae/{aeId}` — Execute a core Canva API action (internal).\n\n## Quick Start\n\n### OpenClaw (Unbrowse) workflow\n- Authenticate in the browser first (no credentials are shipped with this skill).\n- Capture fresh auth locally: run `unbrowse_capture` on an authenticated page for this domain.\n- Execute via backend gate + client browser executor: `unbrowse_replay` with `executionMode=\"backend\"`.\n\nExample:\n```text\nunbrowse_replay { service: \"canva\", executionMode: \"backend\", endpoint: \"GET /{id}\" }\n```\n\nHere are a few examples to get you started using the Canva API:\n\n```typescript\n// Retrieve a Canva design by its ID.\nasync function getDesign(designId: string) {\n  const design = await client.getDesign(designId);\n  return design;\n}\n```\n\n```typescript\n// Retrieve a nested object within a Canva design (e.g., a specific element).\nasync function getElement(designId: string, elementId: string) {\n  const element = await client.getElement(designId, elementId);\n  return element;\n}\n```\n\n```typescript\n// Send tracing data to Canva.  Useful for monitoring API usage and debugging.\nasync function sendTrace(traceData: any) {\n  await client.sendTrace(traceData);\n}\n```\n\n## Additional Notes\n\n**Type:** Reverse-engineered internal API (unofficial)\n**Auth:** Session Token (x-csrf-token)\n**Base URL:** `https://www.canva.com`\n**Captured Auth:** 1 auth headers, 8 session cookies\n\n## About This Skill\n\nThis skill provides access to Canva's internal API — the hidden endpoints that power their web/mobile app.\nThese are NOT official public APIs. They were captured by observing network traffic while using the site.\n\n**Important:**\n- Auth tokens in `auth.json` may expire — re-capture if you get 401 errors\n- Internal APIs can change without notice — endpoints may break\n- Rate limits are unknown — be conservative with request frequency\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\nUse this skill when you need to:\n- Access Canva data without official API access\n- Automate actions on www.canva.com (faster than browser automation)\n- Call the same endpoints the Canva frontend uses\n\n## Quick Start\n\n```typescript\nimport { CanvaClient } from \"./scripts/api.ts\";\n\n// Load captured auth from auth.json\nconst client = await CanvaClient.fromAuthFile(\"auth.json\");\n\n// Make requests to internal endpoints\nconst result = await client.get(\"/endpoint\");\n```\n\n## Captured Authentication\n\nThe `auth.json` file contains credentials extracted from browser traffic:\n- **Auth headers:** 1 (x-csrf-token)\n- **Session cookies:** 8\n\nIf auth expires, re-run `unbrowse_login` or `unbrowse_capture` to refresh tokens.\n\n## Internal Endpoints (11)\n\n\n## Error Handling\n\n```typescript\ntry {\n  const data = await client.get(\"/resource\");\n} catch (err) {\n  if (err.message.includes(\"401\")) {\n    // Auth expired — need to re-capture\n    console.error(\"Auth expired, re-run unbrowse_login\");\n  } else {\n    console.error(\"API error:\", err.message);\n  }\n}\n```\n\nSee [REFERENCE.md](references/REFERENCE.md) for detailed endpoint documentation.\n"
